+## CLI Pipe Execution Harness & Confinement Contract (`cli_pipe`, KB-P5-21, S14.3)
+
+The `agent.runners.cli_pipe` and `agent.runners.repo_snapshot` modules implement the zero-shell, read-only `cli_pipe` execution harness for local CLI agents (`${context} | agy -p` and `codex -p -s read-only`):
+
+1. **Zero-Shell Direct `execve` Execution:**
+   - Subprocesses are spawned strictly with `shell=False` via `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec`, passing target arguments directly after an `nsjail` `--` separator.
+   - Untrusted ticket context (`kb-transition-context/v1`) is transmitted exclusively over child `FD 0 (stdin)` as a spotlighted YAML block scalar and closed with EOF. Untrusted ticket data NEVER enters `argv` or environment variables.
+
+2. **Runtime Policy Gate & Double-Validation:**
+   - Calls `assert_runtime_argv(agent_def)` immediately before spawn. Any banned CLI flag (`--yolo`, `--dangerously-*`, `--full-auto`, `--allow-all-tools`) or unpinned Codex sandbox overrides fail immediately with `CliPolicyError` (`BANNED_CLI_FLAG` or `CODEX_SANDBOX_OVERRIDE`) before touching `nsjail` or staging repo snapshots.
+
+3. **Linux User Namespace Probe & Fail-Closed Sandboxing:**
+   - Calls `probe_nsjail_userns()`. If unprivileged user namespaces (`CLONE_NEWUSER`) or the root-owned `/usr/bin/nsjail` binary are unavailable (e.g. standalone single-container deployments), execution fails closed with `SandboxUnavailableError("SANDBOX_UNAVAILABLE_IN_STANDALONE")` and never executes unsandboxed on the host.
+
+4. **4-Layer Read-Only Repository Confinement:**
+   - When `repo_access_mode == "ro_vfs_mount"`, `RoRepoSnapshotManager` materializes a detached snapshot of `repo_context.head_commit` from `mirror_path` via `git archive` extracted in Python `tarfile` with `filter="data"` (rejecting absolute links, `..`, devices, FIFOs, setuid bits, and outside symlinks).
+   - Generates an `nsjail` protobuf config mounting `/workspace/repo` with `MS_BIND | MS_REC | MS_RDONLY | MS_NODEV | MS_NOSUID | MS_NOEXEC` (`--bindmount_ro` with `noexec,nosuid,nodev`).
+   - Staging directories on the host are cleaned up unconditionally in `finally`.
+
+5. **0000 Secret & Hook Whiteout Overlays:**
+   - Automatically discovers all `.env*`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, `.git/config`, and `.git/hooks` paths across the repository tree.
+   - Overlays each discovered target with a `0000` empty tmpfs mount inside `/workspace/repo` prior to `pivot_root`.
+   - Capped at 256 whiteouts; repositories with > 256 secret files fail closed with `REPO_WHITEOUT_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` rather than leaving any secret unmasked.
+
+6. **Clean Environment & Ephemeral Token Scoping:**
+   - Employs `keep_env: false` to clear host environment. Configures only `PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin`, `HOME=/tmp`, `LANG=C.UTF-8`, and `KANBAN_EPHEMERAL_MCP_TOKEN`.
+   - Host secrets (`DATABASE_URL`, `MASTER_KEK`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) and `LD_PRELOAD` are guaranteed absent.
+   - Ephemeral token buffers are scrubbed/zeroed upon completion.
+
+7. **Caps, Timeouts & Failure Modes:**
+   - Stdout is capped at 1,048,576 bytes (1 MiB; exceeding kills child and raises `CLI_STDOUT_TOO_LARGE`).
+   - Stderr is capped at 262,144 bytes and scrubbed via `scrub_text`.
+   - Timeouts trigger process group `SIGKILL` and raise `GATE_TIMEOUT`.
+   - Non-zero exits without a valid `kb-transition-verdict/v1` payload on stdout raise `CliRunnerExitError` (`CLI_NONZERO_EXIT`).
+
 ## CLI Framework Contract (`kanban-agent`)
 
 The `kanban-agent` command-line interface provides a typed, zero-shell manual validation workbench for local agent evaluation and testing:
